# The Atlas image tag. Leave it unset and compose uses `latest`. The version
# this commit was built, tested and deployed against is in .atlas_version;
# pin to it with:  echo "ATLAS=$(cat .atlas_version)" >> .env
#ATLAS_RAILS_MASTER_KEY=123123
# Cantaloupe as reachable from INSIDE the web container, for server-side
# IIIF info.json reads (manifest dimensions). Browsers use the public
# iiif_host; leave unset when the two are the same. In compose:
#CERBERUS_IIIF_INTERNAL_HOST=http://iiif:8182

# Gated-derivative model. MasterJp2 writes both the capped display JP2 and the
# full-res JP2 to the one derivatives dir Cantaloupe reads, distinguished by an
# `open-`/`gated-` filename prefix; the Cantaloupe delegate serves `open-*`
# freely and requires a signed URL / grant cookie for `gated-*`. The signing
# secret is the HMAC key shared with that delegate — set it (identically on the
# iiif service) to enforce gating; unset means dev serves everything ungated.
#CERBERUS_IIIF_SIGNING_SECRET=change-me-shared-with-cantaloupe-delegate

# Handle (persistent identifier) minting. Atlas mints one per Work at
# /complete and stores it as `handle`; Cerberus only reads it back and links
# it. The local Handle.Net server is an ordinary compose service, so a plain
# `up` starts it and every one of these has a working default. Leave the whole
# block commented out unless you need to change something.
#
# The admin secret authenticates every administrative write. The compose file
# supplies a dev value so a fresh checkout boots; set your own to override it.
# NOTE: .env does no command substitution — HANDLE_ADMIN_SECRET=$(openssl rand
# -hex 16) stores those 23 characters literally. Generate it in your shell and
# paste the result:
#   openssl rand -hex 16
#HANDLE_ADMIN_SECRET=paste-a-generated-hex-string-here
# The prefix the local server is authoritative for. Northeastern's registered
# prefix is 2047; DRSDEV is unregistered and resolves only on that server.
#HANDLE_PREFIX=DRSDEV
# Where a minted handle sends a reader — Cerberus's public host, since Atlas
# does not know it.
#CERBERUS_PUBLIC_BASE=http://localhost:3000
# The resolver Cerberus links a handle against. Defaults to the local server,
# because DRSDEV is in no registry and CNRI's global proxy cannot answer for
# it. Production points this at https://hdl.handle.net for prefix 2047.
#HANDLE_RESOLVER_BASE=http://localhost:8000
